From: Cyryl Sochacki <cyrylsochacki@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:37:31 +0100
Subject: Input: edt-ft5x06 - retry identification after I2C bus recovery

On the LeMaker Banana Pro (Allwinner A20) with the LeMaker LCD panels the
first I2C transfer to the FT5x06 after boot always fails:

  mv64xxx_i2c_fsm: Ctlr Error -- state: 0x2, status: 0x0, addr: 0x38
  edt_ft5x06 2-0038: touchscreen probe failed
  edt_ft5x06 2-0038: probe with driver edt_ft5x06 failed with error -11

The adapter recovers the bus and returns -EAGAIN. Binding the driver again
later works, so retry the identification once on -EAGAIN.

Signed-off-by: Cyryl Sochacki <cyrylsochacki@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
@@ -1273,6 +1273,18 @@ static int edt_ft5x06_ts_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	i2c_set_clientdata(client, tsdata);
 
 	error = edt_ft5x06_ts_identify(client, tsdata);
+	/*
+	 * On some boards (e.g. LeMaker Banana Pro with the LeMaker LCD panels)
+	 * the very first transfer after boot fails with a bus error, as the
+	 * bus is not idle yet. The I2C adapter then recovers the bus and
+	 * returns -EAGAIN, so retry the identification once instead of
+	 * failing the probe.
+	 */
+	if (error == -EAGAIN) {
+		dev_info(&client->dev, "identification failed, retrying\n");
+		usleep_range(10000, 11000);
+		error = edt_ft5x06_ts_identify(client, tsdata);
+	}
 	if (error) {
 		dev_err(&client->dev, "touchscreen probe failed\n");
 		return error;
-- 
